From 40a40213787f8307c884bb05f47d3ea93e60342f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Kiefer <kkiefer@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:34:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] video_dec_drm: accept the documented UI-only invocation

The help text documents video_dec_drm --disable-video and the option
parser supports it, but get_num_context rejects the invocation before
it reaches that parser because there is no video filename and codec.

Allow the UI-only option through the initial argument-count check while
retaining the required arguments for video playback.

Change-Id: If2b8166e451158152a6a64ba70925c6375ed59e0
Upstream-Status: Submitted [NVIDIA internal review]
Signed-off-by: Kurt Kiefer <kkiefer@nvidia.com>
---
 samples/08_video_dec_drm/video_dec_drm_csvparser.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/samples/08_video_dec_drm/video_dec_drm_csvparser.cpp b/samples/08_video_dec_drm/video_dec_drm_csvparser.cpp
index 9a8dfd6..a81b6bc 100644
--- a/samples/08_video_dec_drm/video_dec_drm_csvparser.cpp
+++ b/samples/08_video_dec_drm/video_dec_drm_csvparser.cpp
@@ -129,7 +129,8 @@ get_num_context(int argc, char **argv, int *skip)
         exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);
     }

-    CSV_PARSE_CHECK_ERROR(argc < 3, "Insufficient arguments");
+    CSV_PARSE_CHECK_ERROR(argc < 3 && strcmp(argv[1], "--disable-video"),
+                          "Insufficient arguments");

     if (!strcmp(argv[1], "multi"))
     {
-- 
